  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Chen sets the pace",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "person-yi-chia-chen-identity-0",
        "person-yi-chia-chen-roster-1",
        "person-yi-chia-chen-roster-0"
      ],
      "text": "Yi-Chia Chen remains first on the ARC-AGI-3 public board at 62.96. The top score at the previous Eastern evening close was 59.17; the observed history does not give Chen a comparable personal start point, so that difference is a change in the board’s leading mark, not a certified individual daily gain. Tufa Labs holds second at 56.52, with mtg third at 45. Chen’s verified Kaggle account is threerabbits, also listed on a separate ARC-AGI-2 team."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The chase tightens",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "person-keith-tyser-identity-0",
        "person-keith-tyser-roster-1",
        "person-keith-tyser-roster-0"
      ],
      "text": "Keith Tyser’s ARC-3 entry rose from 69th at the prior close to 13th, its score moving from 32.74 to 37.22. The public roster links the keithtyser handle to this entry; Tyser is also listed on ARC Raiders in ARC-AGI-2, a separate contest and team. The provisional gold cutoff rose from 35.79 to 36.14."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The front group",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "person-jean-francois-puget-identity-0",
        "person-jean-francois-puget-roster-1",
        "person-jean-francois-puget-roster-0",
        "person-jean-francois-puget-archive-0"
      ],
      "text": "Behind mtg, Majkel1337 is fourth at 42.66, NVARC3 fifth at 40.97, and the last dance 🕺 sixth at 39.30. Lord Han Solo is 15th at 36.61. Jean-François Puget’s verified cpmpml account is observed on NVARC3 here and on nvbanana in ARC-AGI-2; the two leaderboard entries have different team IDs. Puget’s 2025 ARC Prize championship belongs to that earlier season."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Beyond the standings",
      "sourceIds": [
        "social-2108936146071777498",
        "social-2108463895128269084"
      ],
      "text": "A new Memento 3 preprint reports clearing all levels of the 25 public ARC-AGI-3 games with a fixed language model and a revisable external rulebook. Those are the authors’ public-set results, not evidence of performance on the unseen competition games. Tufa Labs’ recent playful post about a setback is competition banter; it gives no basis for claims about its resources or current submission."
    }
  ],
